d px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink focus:border-accent sm:order-none sm:w-auto"><option value="0">Etappe 1: Getting started: capitals, numbers, punctuation</option><option value="1">Etappe 2: Lesson 4: Alphabetic Wordsigns</option><option value="2">Etappe 3: Lesson 5: Strong Wordsigns: and, for, of, the, with</option><option value="3">Etappe 4: Lesson 6: Strong Groupsigns: and, for, of, the, with</option><option value="4">Etappe 5: Lesson 7: ch, gh, sh, th, wh (+ Wordsigns child, shall, this, which)</option><option value="5">Etappe 6: Lesson 8: ed, er, ou, ow (+ Wordsign out)</option><option value="6">Etappe 7: Lesson 9: st, ar, ing (+ Wordsign still)</option><option value="7">Etappe 8: Lesson 10: be, con, dis; Shortforms</option><option value="8">Etappe 9: Lesson 11: ea, bb, cc, ff, gg</option><option value="9">Etappe 10: Lesson 12: en, in; Lower Sign Rule</option><option value="10">Etappe 11: Lesson 13: Lower Wordsigns: be, his, was, were, enough, in; Shortforms</option><option value="11">Etappe 12: Lesson 14: Summary of Lower Signs; Shortforms</option><option value="12">Etappe 13: Lesson 15: Dot 5 initial-letter contractions D–M; Shortforms</option><option value="13">Etappe 14: Lesson 16: Dot 5 initial-letter contractions N–U; Shortforms</option><option value="14">Etappe 15: Lesson 17: Dot 5 initial-letter contractions (rest); Shortforms</option><option value="15">Etappe 16: Lesson 18: Dots 4-5: upon, word, these, those, whose</option><option value="16">Etappe 17: Lesson 19: Dots 4-5-6: cannot, had, many, spirit, world, their</option><option value="17">Etappe 18: Lesson 20: Final-letter groupsigns: ance, ence, sion, tion, less, ness</option><option value="18">Etappe 19: Lesson 21: Final-letter groupsigns: ound, ong, ount, ment</option><option value="19">Etappe 20: Lesson 22: Final-letter groupsigns: ful, ity</option></select><span data-hinweis-anker="tipp-ra7" hidden=""></span></span><span class="relative inline-flex"><button type="button" class="btn-secondary btn-toggle" aria-label="Nächste Etappe" aria-describedby="tipp-ra8"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><span data-hinweis-anker="tipp-ra8" hidden=""></span></span></div></div></div><div class="space-y-4"><details class="blatt-karte rounded-xl border border-accent/30 bg-accent-soft p-3" open=""><summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Diese Kürzungen üben wir hier: <span class="font-normal text-ink-soft">but · can · do · every · from · go · have · just · knowledge · like · more · not · people · quite · rather · so · that · us · very · will · it · you · as</span></summary><p class="mb-3 mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">Some letters, standing all on their own, mean a whole word! b means but, c means can, k means knowledge. One little cell — a whole word.</p><ul tabindex="-1" aria-label="Meine Tasten: Kürzungen dieser Welt" class="m-0 flex list-none flex-wrap gap-3 p-0 outline-none"><li class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-surface-sunken px-3 py-2"><div aria-hidden="true" class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1"><span class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">but</span><div class="flex flex-wrap items-start gap-2 "><svg role="img" aria-label="Punkte 1, 2" data-zustand="neutral" viewBox="0 0 60 90" width="18.666666666666664" height="28"><circle cx="18" cy="15" r="10" fill="rgb(var(--c-ink))" stroke="none" stroke-width="0"></circle><circle cx="18" cy="45" r="10" fill="rgb(var(--c-ink))" stroke="none" stroke-width="0"></circle><circle cx="18" cy="75" r="8.5" fill="none" stroke="rgb(var(--c-hairline))" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.7"></circle><circle cx="42" cy="15" r="8.5" fill="none" stroke="rgb(var(--c-hairline))" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.7"></circle><circle cx="42" cy="45" r="8.5" fill="none" stroke="rgb(var(--c-hairline))" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.7"></circle><circle cx="42" cy="75" r="8.5" fill="none" stroke="rgb(var(--c-hairline))" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.7"></circle></svg></div></div><span class="sr-only">but: Punkte 1, 2 ⠃</span></